course: dictionary
lesson: 8187
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word rest has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one the writer means. «The rest of the class went home.» Here rest means the other people or things, the part that is left over after some have gone.
explain: Rest can also mean a time to stop and relax. «Muscles grow over months with exercise, food and rest.» Here rest is what your body needs in order to get better.
explain: To rest means to relax, or to lie or lean on something. «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes.» Try your meaning in the sentence, and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Rest can mean the part that is left over, as in «the rest of the herd».
fact: Rest can mean a time to stop and relax, as in «take a rest».
fact: «At rest» means not moving.
fact: In music, «a rest is a counted silence and is part of the bar».
fact: Rest helps the body get better after exercise.
exercise: «The rest of the class went home.» What does rest mean here? | * The other people or things | A loud noise | To lean on something | A time to sleep
exercise: «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes.» What does rest mean in this sentence? | To count the beats | To leave something behind | To run fast across the plain | * To relax, or lie or lean on something
exercise: In music, «a rest is a counted silence». What is a rest? | A very long note | A loud drumbeat | A type of dance | * A counted silence that is part of the bar
test: «Muscles grow over months with exercise, food and rest.» What does rest mean in this sentence? | To lean on a rock | * A time to stop and relax | A kind of herb | A part left over
test: «Springboks leap high to warn the rest of the herd.» What does rest mean here? | * The other members | Stiff legs | To relax | Sleepy
exam: Which phrase means not moving? | * At rest | The rest of | Take a rest | Rest on
